{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "## Carl Bot Commands\n- **?pr** - Player gold and XP rewards\n- **?sr** - Summary writing rewards\n- **?dr** - Rewards for DM’ing a game\n- **?c** - Quick access to important chronicler pages\n## Avrae\nCommonly used commands are listed below, please use the **!help** for more.\n### Basic Commands\nWhere x = number of dice, y = die size, c = modifier, z = number of iterrations.\n- !r xdy+c - for rolling dice\n- !rr z xdy+c - for rolling multiple iterations\n- !r 2dykh1+c - for advantage\n- !r 2dykl1+c - for disadvantage\n### Setting Avrae to only 2024 rules\n!csettings version 2024\n### Lookup Commands\nTo find information about official content.\n- !background name\n- !class name level\n- !classfeat name\n- !condition|status name\n- !feat name \n- !item name\n- !monimage name\n- !monster name\n- !race name\n- !racefeat name\n- !rule|reference name\n- !spell name\n- !subclass name\n### Setting up a character:\n- !import DDB char link - for importing your character to the bot  \n- !character - for choosing the right character  \n- !update - for make sure everything is up to good as new  \n- !check ability - for making an ability check  \n- !action - for choosing an action to take  \n- !attack - for attacking with your char  \n- !cast - for casting a spell  \n- !spellbook - for checking which spells are prepared  \n- !g lr - for long resting  \n- !g sr - for short resting\n## Avrae Aliases\nTo text RP as our respective characters, we use character aliases created in the Avrae bot. Following are the instructions to make one for your character. Well, it's quite simple, in essence there are only 2 steps.  \n\nBut first of all, what is this and why do we need it? Very simply speaking it will provide us with character speech bubbles to use in text RP. Something like this -\n\n![Avrae Alias Example](https://i.ibb.co/fdNzjtJb/image.png)\n### Step 1: Copy the following code\nYou need to copy the code below in your character token thread. Just don't press enter yet, keep it in the typing box.\n\n```\n!alias <character_alias> embed -desc %*% -thumb <link_to_character_image> -title \"<character_name>\" -footer \"<character_title>\"\n```\n### Step 2: Fill details in the code:\nFor all the following details remember you have to take out the <> signs as well.\n- **Character alias**: Imagine this alias as a box, this is the name you will take to make Avrae use this box.\n- For the speech bubbles to appear, you have to type in the beginning of a new message `!<character alias> Awesome shit your character says:`\n- As you have to type this again and again, I would suggest keeping it something short and memorable\n- For e.g.: For my own character Zagreus Nyxborn this is just a simple `z`\n- **Link to character image**: Just copy the link to your character token and paste it here\n- **Character name**: Type in whatever you want your character's name to appear as in the speech bubble. Just keep it within the `\"Double qoutes\"`\n- **Character title**: Type in any small tidbit of flavor you want to add to your character's speech bubble. Again, keep it within the `\"Double qoutes\"`\n- Press enter and let the bot do its magic!\n", "category": "Getting started", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🤖\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Instructions on how to use avrae and carl bots.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "2187d5ef-fe7f-5609-b6fa-7e943dab2011", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "bots-guide", "status": "published", "title": "Bots Guide", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "Any conflict between characters need to happen with consultation with the three parties involved: **the two conflicting player sided parties and the Dungeon Master**. Any character vs character conflict without a DM involved will be considered null and void. Whenever a character conflict is brewing in session first thing you must do is take 2 minutes above the table to discuss what may happen next, called a **conflict timeout**. The DM or the players can call for this break - this cannot be denied.\n\nWhen calling for the conflict timeout go over the following points:\n\n1. The players involved - from all sides of the conflicts - must be willing participants of this process. This includes the DM.\n2. Any un-consenting participants must have a way of avoiding such a conflict. If you are the DM who do not consent, the players must provide a way to delay the conflict.\n3. The resolution or likely ways it might go should be discussed by the players and the DM must be informed BEFORE it is carried out at the table.\n4. The course of action and its character repercussions must be declared - mostly what action might make what character turn hostile/neutral/friendly.\n\n### Note:\n- On Discord under Channels and Roles, you can pickup a role called Character Conflict, you have this role you are assumed to be eager to participate in most character vs character conflicts.\n- Conflicts need not be combat; they may be any course of action that may lead to disagreements - strong or weak - among the party members. \n- The conflict must be initiated in a safe environment and any sly/underhanded moves will be cause for concern.\n- Outside of session conflicts may be mediated by any third-party DM or Mod.\n- The ethos of the server is heroic fantasy, even players with Character Conflict on are not supposed to be evil.\n- Anyone found not adhering to the rules & guidelines mentioned above will be warned/reprimanded at first. If the behavior persists, they will be kicked from the server.\n", "category": "Conflict & others", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🫯\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules about handling character vs character conflicts\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "a82ee3e5-9fb1-5ebd-94a4-b041e2567d5d", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "character-conflict", "status": "published", "title": "Character Conflict", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "This is that part in video games where you spend hours customizing your character, so this guide is going to cover the absolute essentials and get out of your way. Let's cook!\n## Step 1 - Join our Content Sharing Links\nFor this server we make characters using D&D beyond and all the content you need access to, for making your character is available in the following links. Here are the steps to join them before you start making your character.\n- Sign in to D&D beyond and make sure you have atleast 1 character slot free on this account.\n- Click on one of the following links - **[1](<https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/58762161238231274>) [2](<https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/58762173527712966>) [3](<https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/58762513847611632>) [4](<https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/63179264049878249>) [5](<https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/65262412999464366>) [6](https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/70844082585712784) [7](https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/70844143526549772) [8](https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/70844163820023200) [9](https://www.dndbeyond.com/campaigns/join/7084417261141498)**\n- You should see something like this\n![DDB Content Sharing Link Page](https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/1553333667349270528/1553333697267368076/image.png?ex=6ab8de3c&is=6ab78cbc&hm=f6ad6d6eeefc7ffae7e9ffd144235b8b730b5fd3b2be3d86801847ea995d2446&=&format=webp&quality=lossless)\n- Click **Create Character**, and off you go!\n### Known Issues\nSometimes when you click on one of these links you will get an error message that says something to the effect of \"Limit Reached\" or \"Campaign Full\", or in other cases even when you join and there is no error you might not see all the content available in the link, in such a situation just join another one of the links provided.\n\n## Step 2 - Home page\nYou will find yourself on a new page with a bunch of toggles and settings. Just do the changes mentioned here and leave everything else as is!\n- Put in your character name\n- Turn on the **Homebrew, 5.5e Core Rules, 5.5e Expanded Rules**, turn off everything else.\n- Turn on only **Grimhollow** content in the **Partnered Content**. (Only the spells from grimhollow are allowed on the server.)\n- Change **Advancement Type** to **XP**\n- Change **Character Privacy** to **Public**\nAll done! Click on the  ` 〉` to go to the next section.\n\n## Step 3 - Classes, Backgrounds and Species\nThe next three pages are all you, spend as much time as you want and make the hero you would love to play.\n### Available Classes\n- All classes that you can see are available except for the **Monster Hunter**.\n### Available Subclasses\n- Make sure you are **Level 3**\n- All subclasses listed under **5.5e Core Rules & 5.5e Expanded Rules** are available, the grimhollow subclasses are not.\n### Available Backgrounds\n- All backgrounds listed under **5.5e Core Rule** are available and only **Familiar Trainer** from **5.5e Expanded Rules** is available.\n- Assign the stat bonuses from your background\n### Available Species\n- All species listed under **5.5e Core Rule** are available except for **Elves**, under **5.5e Expanded Rules** only **Dhampir, Lupin and Hexblood** are available, under **Homebrew** only **Metalborn Dwarves and Cyclops** are available.\n- If you want to read more about what each species, background, class and subclass represents in Weeping, you can refer to the Flavor Profile Document.\n## Step 4 - Abilities & Equipment\n- Choose Point Buy as your **Generation Method** and assign stats accordingly.\n- Choose the last option from all equipment sections that you get from your class and backgrounds.\n- Click on **Add starting equipment.**\n- Click on the  ` 〉` to go to the next section. \n- Click on **View Character Sheet**.\n- Copy your D&D Beyond Link from the browser.\n## Multiple characters!\nYup, you read that right. **You can make not one but Two characters when you begin playing in this westmarch**. It is optional but available at your pleasure. This number might even increase in the future depending on many problems you guys solve or create. The relationship between all your characters is left up to you to decide they can be strangers, siblings, friends and whatever else your fantasy takes you to!\n\nJust know that one of the many intents of us allowing multiple characters is so that in the early days of the westmarch at lower levels when characters are at a higher risk of death, you may still retain information and knowledge learned through that character on your second character without breaking immersion. Mechanically both characters are separate entitles, with xp, gold, items etc tracked differently. They need to be distinct personalities from each other and recognizable as such.\n## Step 5 - Chronicler Profile\nNow that your character is made you must add it to your profile, so you can sign up to games with it.\n- Click on your **Profile Icon** in the upper right corner.\n- Click on **Characters**.\n- Put up your **Character Name**, select the **Lightfall** region and **Solarii** as your backstory, paste the DDB link and write out a description of what your character looks like and save.\n- Your character will automatically be sent to verification, all you must do now is go to the [Verify Channel](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1553653409553457232) in discord and tag @verify with your character name to let them know that your character is in the verification pool. \n- If everything is okay they will verify your character or else they will help you rectify any misteps but soon enough you will approved and ready to play.\n\n## and… we are done!\n", "category": "Character", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🦸🏻\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Character Creation Rules.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "cf74ccf8-06f7-599b-b966-a60ef56ab8f5", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "character-creation", "status": "published", "title": "Character Creation", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "Re-specs are reserved for fresh characters and genuine mistakes that make the game not fun to play. Re-specs are per character, and all characters qualify for re-specs. However, re-specs can be denied if certain characters are involved in a story.\n## 1. For new characters\nFor characters having played less than 4 games, you can change everything about the character except the following. You don't need approval for these respecs.\n- Name (real name)\n- Species\n\n## 2. For characters of any level\nYou can re-spec only once. If you wish to do a re-spec, mention your reason and tag @veirfy in the verify channel. Only on approval is your re-spec granted. There are further restrictions on re-specs this way. You can change everything about the character except:\n- Name (real name)\n- Species\n- Class\n- Background\n\n## ReSpecs - Multi-classing\nCharacters who are multi-classes must maintain the same class composition aka a `cleric x fighter` remains a `cleric x fighter`. They can shift which class was the first class and how many levels you allocate to each class. Other rules remain as is.\n", "category": "Character", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🔨\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules for Re-specing your characters.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "17103e95-d8ed-5195-a3ea-ed2ede32a935", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "character-respec", "status": "published", "title": "Character Respec", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "## Flavor\nAs Solarii are people who have been giving a second life to serve the divine purpose they can never stop doing so, they must serve. If service becomes too much for them, the Temple of Apollo preaches that every Solarii carries a mote of Apollo's light, a small piece of the god that was only ever lent and is meant to be returned. \n\nWhen a Solarii's road ends, they take part in a divine ritual and give the mote back willingly. In that act they become one with Apollo and the great tree.\n\nA light in the Solarii's own color slips out and begins to climb the tree's bark, rising slowly through the trunk and the boughs until it reaches the canopy. There it scatters into countless sparks that drift out over the city and fight against the weeping. The Temple holds that this is the truest end a Solarii can hope for: not a fading, but a continuing, with every gifted light still working against the rain.\n\nThat the given are not gone. In time, the living will be able to enter the ritual room and commune with the spirit of Solarii who gave up their light, and feel them in the warmth of the tree.\n## Mechanics\nIf you want to retire your character, you can simply go to your character profile and click on **Retire Character** to do so. This unfortunately is not a world where a peaceful life in a far off location is available, if your character retires they have two choices - Become one with the tree and pass into the light of apollo or change what kind of service they are providing under the light and become one of the many support staff that keep the city of lightfall running. \n\nIf your character chooses to become one with the tree, you may RP out visions that they might send their acquaintances from the afterlife, these visions are meant for you to be able to say any important words that might be left, disperse any information you have etc. Use these visions tastefully and respect the departure of your soul from this world.\n\nIf your character chooses to change their service to light and instead choose a peaceful existence within the city of lightfall, they are mostly busy fulfilling their duties. You may cameo in the text rp channels once every month. Respect your characters decision to seek out life away from adventuring and keep your cameos short and to the point.\n", "category": "Character", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🏞️\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules and Flavor for Character Retirement\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "379cb304-aed2-58a7-a1db-fbd48dc7bb6f", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "character-retirement", "status": "published", "title": "Character Retirement", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "These are the common rules by which we engage with our community, please read and refer to them whenever disputes arise between any entities. They are here to ensure that this community is a place where everyone has a good time.\n**This is strictly an 18 and over server.**\n### 1. Be respectful\nYou must respect all users, regardless of your liking towards them. Treat others the way you want to be treated.\n### 2. No Inappropriate Language\nThe use of profanity should be kept to a minimum. However, any derogatory language towards any user is prohibited. Respect the difference between banter and pointed insults.\n### 3. No spamming\nDon't send a lot of small messages right after each other. Do not disrupt chat by spamming.\n### 4. No pornographic/adult/other NSFW material\nThis is a community server and not meant to share this kind of material.\n### 5. No spam advertisements\nWe do not tolerate any kind of advertisements, whether it be for other communities or streams. You can post your content in the media channel and dedicated links and promos channel.\n### 6. No offensive names and profile pictures\nYou will be asked to change your name or picture if the staff deems them inappropriate.\n### 7. Server Raiding\nRaiding or mentions of raiding are not allowed.\n### 8. Direct & Indirect Threats\nThreats to other users of DDoS, Death, DoX, abuse, and other malicious threats are absolutely prohibited and disallowed.\n### 9. Follow the Discord Community Guidelines\nYou can find them here: <https://discordapp.com/guidelines>\n### 10. Content guidelines\nAll ideas/media/content/personalities created or ideated, such as characters, NPCs, proper nouns etc., in the server is in the public domain.\n## Gaming Rules\nHow we play games is how we do everything, make sure your style of gaming is communicative and collaborative. \n### 1. Text based role play \nAll text based RP channels should be utilized in a family friendly manner, Erotic Role Play is not encouraged.\n### 2. The table is a safe space for everyone\nIf you observe behavior that targets **Individuals/groups/communities** in any shape or form, [report](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1285218484216795247).\n### 3. The flow of the session is precious. \nIf you disagree with a DMs ruling on mechanics, specially in cases of **Bias/unfairness/revenge**, we advise you to communicate your concerns with the DM at the end of the session or get in touch with the admin team by raising a ticket as shown below.\n### 4. Respect cross server lines and veils\nIt is our shared duty as players and DMs to strictly respect the [server lines and veils](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1285218270068346902). Any violations ought to be [reported immediately](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1285218484216795247).\n### 5. When emotions run high, situations get complicated. \nA mod reserves the right to **Mute/deafen/timeout** until an unfolding situation can be moved to a safe space for evaluation and resolution. This may include similar treatment for any/all parties involved in the short term.\nIf you see any of these violated anywhere on the server, to any degree, we rely on you to report such activities so they can be addressed appropriately.\n## Server Wide Lines and Veils\nThe server uses the MCDM safety toolkit for lines and veils. These themes must be strictly Avoided, during sessions or in any of the text Role Play channels. Any violations should be [reported.](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1285218484216795247)\nIt is important to note that lines and veils are additive, as much as your lines and veils is to be respected, so is anyone else's at the table. \n> P.S. Please ensure that your lines and veils are known to the table and the DM is particularly informed of them in a timely manner.\n- Link to the full post: <https://www.patreon.com/posts/announcing-mcdm-73512191>\n- Download link: <https://mcdm.gg/SafetyToolkit>\n- Server Lines & Veils Full Document: [Weeping Lines and Veils](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1553333667349270528/1554198422490189824/Weeping_Lines_and_Veils.pdf?ex=6abc0393&is=6abab213&hm=04f084eb8002167be1b8af478d2da3d90a881f89e191d66a4fd0cfa2a0fbdd76&)\n- Server Lines & Veils Summary - Veil on (Abortion, Childbirth, Miscarriage, Pregnancy Complications, Still Birth) and veils on sexual content (Jokes about sex or genitalia, Kissing, Having sex, Between PCs, Between PCs and NPCs)\n\n**These are subject to change as the server progresses, the admin team reserves the right to do so.**\n## Final Disclaimer\nThe Admins and Mods will Mute/Kick/Ban per discretion. If you feel mistreated raise a ticket and we will resolve the issue. All Channels will have pinned messages explaining what they are there for and how everything works. If you don't understand something, feel free to ask!\n\n**Your presence in this community implies accepting these rules, including all further changes. These changes might be made at any time and any such change in the server rules will be announced in advance.**\n## Report an Issue\nUse [this tool](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1367600132492754966) to raise a complaint, or get in touch with moderators for any/all purposes. This is a direct line upstairs.\nOpen a ticket here to get in touch with the moderators and other community managers, this raises an anonymous ticket where information can be shared safely.\n**In case of violations by any of the authoritative figures, we recommend you DM the issue to the non-offending mods, this is reserved for such cases only.**\n", "category": "Groups & places", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"👪\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules everyone in the community must follow.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "05d279c0-bc6f-5a97-9718-f2e954d0fab5", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "community-rules", "status": "published", "title": "Community Rules", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "## Arc Theme\nThe theme of the current story arc is exploration. These are the kinds of stories the server wants and mechanically supports right now. We are in a Points of Light setting, that means that other than Lightfall there is no other civilization that exists (That we know about), no villages, no towns, nothing. The world is covered in darkness and weeping and Lightfall is the only bastion of light, from whence solarii step out to look for the Prism of Hope, an ancient lost artifact that is prophesized to give civilization the strength to survive.\n## Map\nIn order to tell a good exploration story, you must understand the map and it's mechanics.\n![Numbered Hex Map](https://i.ibb.co/Q3L05Wr0/Lightfall-Hex-Map.png)\n### Central Hex\n- The very center of this map, Hex number LFC1001, is where Lightfall is situated. This is the bastion of civilization, all games begin here and all solarii must return here at the end of session. \n- The light of the great tree protects the entire hex of lightfall from weeping, there are no monsters here, just humanoids. Stories related to social turmoil and chill or party games can be ran in this hex, but essentially this zone is mostly supposed to be conflict free.\n### Hex Numbering Convention\n- All the other hexes are where the games must happen, first the hex number naming convention is Region Name - Ring Number - Hex Number. Example - LFR1001\n- Hexes are numbered in rings around the central hex, the first hex of the ring is always in the cardinal north of central hex and then the numbering goes clockwise.\n### Hex States\n- Each hex has three possible states it can be in - Locked, Unlocked and Mapped.\n- At the beginning of the server only the central hex and ring 1 are unlocked, everything else is locked.\n- **Games can only be DMed in Unlocked Hexes.**\n- When 3 games have been ran on a hex it is considered mapped. When a hex is mapped it unlocks the 6 hexes adjacent to it.\n- You can check the current state of the map at [Maps](/map).\n## Monster Sources\nThese are the books from which you can choose monsters for your games. Dragons are not allowed to be run without express permission from paper. \n- Flee Mortals\n- Monster Manual\n- Tome of Beasts 1-3\n- Conflux creatures\n- Any non-adventure WOTC official book\n- Grimhollow Bestiary\n- https://www.reddit.com/r/bettermonsters/  Stat blocks provided by the user **MARK** only.\nTo add these on 5etools:\n- Go to filters\n- Click on core/supplements to get the non-adventure WOTC official book\n- In partnered, find two grimhollow books, flee mortals and ToB1'2023\n- Then, go to utilities -> homebrew manager in the top toolbar\n  - Click on Get Homebrew\n  - Add the following sources: conflux creatures (same as bettermonsters mostly), anything with grimhollow in the name, tome of beasts 2 and tome of beasts 3.\n## Cursed Monsters\nThe biggest reason why there are no civilizations outside of Lightfall, is the curse of weeping. Any Humanoid or Beast type creature that stays outside in the rain is mutated by it. They turn into animalistic monsters whose only instinct is to soak themselves in the waters of weeping to keep growing and to capture and bring new targets to get cursed.\n\nThese are the standard monsters of this world, the following mechanics tell you how to adapt an existing humanoid or beast statblock to a cursed statblock. The higher in CR you get the smarter and more cunning these monsters become, but their goals remain the same. Kaijus from pacific rim are a great behavioral and visual inspiration for the cursed.\n\n![Cursed Mechanics](https://i.ibb.co/Gf0RFdhV/Dn-D-Notes-45.png)\n## Homebrew\n- Making Minor Alterations and Adding Traits as listed in the DMG [here](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#CreatingaCreature), is allowed for all DMs.\n- If you homebrew a statblock further or make one from the ground up, you must show it to a **DM Mentor** and get their approval.\n- In general if you need help with Homebrew or are unsure about it, reach out to DM mentors.\n## CR Limits\nThe CR limit of monsters you can have in your games is directly proportional to the hex distance from Lightfall.\n\n| Ring | CR Limit |\n| ---- | -------- |\n| 1- 2 | 4        |\n| 3    | 6        |\n| 4    | 9        |\n| 5    | 11       |\n| 6    | 13       |\n| 7-8  | 16       |\n## Story System\nThis is how you create persistent elements for the server. \n### Earning SP\nYou earn story points in the following ways.\n- All DMs start with 10 SP.\n- Hosting a session - 1 point (2 points if it’s a game associated with a quest request)\n- Collaborating with the DM/Server - 1 point\n\n> Collaborating encapsulates using another DMs lore, taking advice from them about mechanics/monsters, using quest-hooks created by directors, running a regional finale game etc. Basically, anytime you as the DM feel you have meaningfully collaborated with another DM, please take the additional SP!\n### Spending SP\nYou spend story points on creating Features and Villains. \n## Features\nFeatures are permanent blocks of worldbuilding you get to add to the setting. Anything that is not a Feature is going to last only for the game it was used in, a feature is designed for repeated use and long term storage, not just by you but other DMs as well.\n\n**Each hex can have a maximum of 4 features.**\n\nTo add a feature just mention the feature type in [this channel](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1556830030003445821) and mention the expenditure of SP to get the claim.\n### Feature Types\n \n| Feature Type         | SP Cost | Description                                                             |\n| -------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Forsaken Ruins       | 1       | Empty old ruins, good for exploration and hiding loot                   |\n| Natural Feature      | 1       | A noticeable natural feature, good for exploration                      |\n| Dungeon              | 3       | Classic Dungeons, good for combats and skill challenges                 |\n| Monster Civilization | 3       | A civilization of monsters, with a base of operations, defenses etc     |\n| Monster Band         | 2       | A roaming band of monsters that can always be encountered in this area. |\n### Creating Features\n- Once you have spent the SP to add a feature.\n- Go to [Maps](/map)\n- Click on the Unlocked Hex where you wish to place your feature\n- Click on New Entry\n- Provide as much details about your feature as you can. This is where other DMs and players will be able to view the information about your feature.\n## Villains\nTo claim a villain just link the stat block in [this channel](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1556830030003445821) and mention the expenditure of SP to get the claim.\n### Villain Hierarchy\nMonster < Captain < Nemesis.\n- All captains are monsters. All nemeses are captains.\n- That means any rules that apply to monsters also apply to villains, unless they have a specific rule which overrides the general. Same for villains and nemesis.\n### Villain Actions\nVillain actions are similar to legendary actions with the following exceptions:\n\n> A creature can use only one villain action per round (as such, villain actions tend to be more powerful than legendary actions). Each villain action can only be used once during a combat encounter.\n\nLike legendary actions, a creature can't use villain actions if incapacitated or otherwise unable to take actions.\n### Captain\n- SP Cost: CR/2 (Rounded Down)\n- Villain Actions: 1\n- Allowed Homebrew:\n    - AC can be increased up to +2.\n    - Can add new bonus actions which can buff the villain or debuff the heroes\n    - Can add new reactions which can let the villain reposition, command an ally or avoid damage\n### Nemesis\nPrerequisite: Must have DM mentor permission\n- **SP Cost**: CR\n- Villain Actions: 3\n- Allowed Homebrew:\n    - HP becomes max of hit dice.\n    - Can add any new actions, so long as the damage output is similar to other actions that stat block has.\n    - Gains 1 uncommon permanent item and 2 uncommon consumables items.\n## Reward System\nThis is how you add rewards for players in your games. For each game you DM you gain reward points (RP) equal to the ring number your game is ran on.\n\nExample - Game on Ring 2, has 2 reward points. Game on Ring 8 will have 8 points.\n\nYou spend reward points to create the reward pool of your game, using the following table to do so.\n\n| Reward               | RP Cost |\n| -------------------- | ------- |\n| Rune Relic           | 1       |\n| Common Item Recipe   | 1       |\n| 5d8 Gold             | 2       |\n| Common Item          | 2       |\n| Plate Relic          | 2       |\n| Blade Relic          | 3       |\n| Uncommon Item Recipe | 4       |\n| Uncommon Item        | 6       |\n| Rare Item Recipe     | 8       |\nYou may spend your RP in whatever combinations you wish. For example a game with 4 RP could have 2 plate relics or 4 rune relics or 1 blade relic and 1 rune relic.\n\n**Flavor Note** - They are pieces of ancient technology from the Age of Heroes, that the Solarii are uncovering and crudely repurposing for their own purposes, feel free to add as much flavor and personality to each relic and magic items that the players find. Additionally Gold is rarer in this setting as compared to other fantasy settings, the RP cost of the gold reflects the same.\n\nPlease do not just give out rewards at the end of your games, let the players find them in the world. They will respect your story more for your efforts to save their immersion.\n\nAs for Recipes, check out [Magic Items](/rules/guides/magic-items) for a more detailed overview on those, but if you are adding a recipe as a reward to your game, you must roll to figure out which one it is. In case you land on a recipe already unlocked roll again.\n- `!r 1d64` for Common Items\n- `!r 1d152` for Uncommon Items\n- `!r 1d180` for Rare Items\n## DM Rewards\nFor every game you DM you gain 1000 xp and 15 gold. You may divide this between your characters as you wish. \n\nThe XP accumulates but DM's characters only get to level up when they play a game. This means, if you have enough XP accumulated, each game can be a level up for your character. \n\nAdditionally if you collab with another DM and use a Feature they established in one of the encounters in your game, you gain 500 bonus XP for that quest and Any DM who writes a DM summary for their games gains an additional 500 xp for that game.\n", "category": "Systems", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🛠️\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules for DMs to run games in this community.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "eeae0988-2c39-50c1-b661-e59eb855b7ae", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "dm-mechanics", "status": "published", "title": "DM Mechanics", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "![A Happpy DM should look like this - Image credits to Irfan.](https://i.ibb.co/v6tmF8mN/Irfan-DM.webp)\n*If westmarching offers death to scheduling issues, it offers life to DM collaboration - Parsec*\n## My Introduction\nHello DMs, I am Ashwin or Mortal on discord, I am the game designer and community manager for this wonderful little corner of escapism. I have a tendency to ramble but you got games to DM, so I am going to keep this as to the point as possible. Let's cook.\n\nThis guide will equip you with all the context you need to know about DMing in this community. It is written in way that would benefit complete beginners and veterans both. The actual mechanics and rules that DMs need have been collected on a seperate [DM Mechanics](/rules/guides/dm-mechanics) page just so you can more easily find them on regular basis.\n## Why DM here?\nDMing is weird, it has its origins in being a refree for wargames, that is what the role began as - an non biased adjudicator of rules, but D&D changed it. They made the DM not just the adjudicator of the rules but also the director of drama. Over the last few decades, this is what modern day DMing has become the one responsible for the pacing of the story, the hook that keeps the table playing, the next plot beat or adventure.\n\nI say DMing is wierd because this is such a position of service, you are the background chorus to 5-7 star singers, yet you are controlling the flow of the symphony. This is an unequal amount of power and responsiblity, if a player is missing the game may go on, if the DM is missing it can not.\n\nThis means the DMs are also naturally responsible for the scheduling of these games as it based on their prep that the game exists or doesn't. Here in lies the problem, because well the people who are enthusiastic to be DMs, want to spend their time coming up with plots, puzzles and grand betrayals. They do not wish to spend their time dealing with scheduling conflicts. \n\nThe second problem most DMs deal with it is that they have a specific story, plot, adventure or idea in mind but they don't have the time or energy to flesh out the rest of world needed to support a ttrpg session. Those of them that do start fleshing it out, contract worldbuilder's disease and instead of running games spend months or years callibrating the right setting and details for their idea to flourish in. Basically what most DMs need is for someone to do a lot of the grunt work and get out of the way so that they can simply start running games.\n\n**Enter - Living Chronicles. The community with hundreds of players and dozens of DMs all operating in the same world.** Basically whenever you want a game to happen, it will. The world and all of its details are created and maintained by our admin team so you can focus on doing what matters to you.\n## Game Philosophy\nInterconnected Episodic Heroic Fantasy. Those are the keywords, let's get into what they actually mean.\n\n**Interconnected** - The games that happen in this server are all part of the same world. This allows DMs to do something that they can never do in campaigns, collaborate with other DMs. Most of the time DMing is a lonely job, where you are the arbitator of fun and chaos for a group of friends, important but always detached. This community provides you with a whole group of DMs that you can bring into your plans that you can build stories together with. You will notice further down in the story system mechanics designed to highlight collaboration between DMs. We encourage you to tell stories through one shots that are connected to each other, we encourage you to be inspired by another DM's game and collaborate with them to make a connected game. This tapestry of stories is what we are here to tell.\n\n**Episodic** - Meaning we here in the community believe in small self contained stories that connect to each other with lore and implications but can themselves be enjoyed as singular experiences. **When you are designing games for this community, make sure that at the end of each game there is narrative room for the players to come back home.** This is the greatest change between DMing here and elsewhere. Think of the games you run here as 1 episode of a web series, or a movie in the MCU, which is a part of the greater narrative but is a complete story in of itself.\n\n**Heroic** - The base assumption is that the players are heroic individuals, they should be relied upon to do and be good. To face challenges that feel impossible for the normal people to overcome, and need efforts above and beyond the call of duty to have effect.\n\n**Fantasy** - The core setting of Weeping is melting pot of a lot of different fantasies by design, your classical tolkien fantasy, a little bit of steampunk, a little bit of fantasy western, a little bit of eastern inspired fantasy. Most of what you want to do in such a medium is possible, the only fantasies not really supported are cyberpunk and sci fi stories. If you are ever in doubt about your ideas reach out to the @DMMentors and they will gladly help you out.\n\n## DMG Extracts\nDid you know that the actual company who publishes D&D also publishes an official Dungeon Master's Guide? Did you know that most DMs never read through this book at all? Well worry not, we have done most of the work for you and found sections that would be helpful for you to know about, instead of reading the book cover to cover (or never even trying.)\n\nThe following segment has sections of the DMG linked to the official DMG pages in DDB. If you don't own a copy of the DMG on DDB yourself, quickly head on over to the [Character Creation Guide](https://chronicler.smokebombstudios.com/rules/guides/character-creation) and join one of the content sharing links there with an existing character, this will give you access to the DMG.\n### [1.3 Session Preparation](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/the-basics#PreparationTime)\nThis chapter tells you to succinctly prepare for a session depending on how much time you have to do so. It really helps you realize what parts you need to focus on to get a game going and what elements can be skipped or trimmed.\n### 1.7 Ensuring Fun for all\nAt its very core D&D is supposed to an experience enjoyed by everyone present. You might be telling the most gruesome, dark story of sadness and despair but that story only has value if it is a “Fun” experience for everyone at the table. In this respect, these three subtopics became pillars around which players and dms engage.\n- [Mutual respect](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/the-basics#MutualRespect)\n- [Intra-party conflict](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/the-basics#IntrapartyConflict)\n- [Expectations](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/the-basics#SettingExpectations)\n### [2.2 Faster combat](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#SpeedingCombat)\nCombat is one of the three core pillars of the game and so we encounter a lot of it. The game is incredibly vast in the mechanics and as such combat can become cumbersome and slow, which then breaks immersion in what is supposed to a fast paced exchange of deadly blows. This section helps DMs and players streamline their combat flow to make it fast\n### [2.4 Narration](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#Narration)\nTechniques to build the atmosphere and flow of game, if you have been DMing for a bit and want to take it to the next step, this would be the recommended reading\n### [2.5 Resolving outcomes](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#ResolvingOutcomes)\nThis is one of the core parts of the game. D&D is just a conversation, where the players tell you what they want to do and you have to adjudicate what the results would be, this section provides you with the details of the how to do this in D&D 2024 mechanically.  \n### [2.6 Social interactions](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#RunningSocialInteraction)\nAdvice on running roleplay encounter with your beloved NPCs.\n### [2.7 Exploration](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#RunningExploration)\nThis section, is once again one of those important bits that DMG says, which will elevate your game experience quite a lot. This is going to 70% of your session time.\n### [2.8 Combat](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/running-the-game#RunningCombat)\nNot going to say much here, 75% of the rules are about this. Glean and try to retain as much of this section as you can.\n### [3.1 Alignment](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#MonsterAlignment)\nWhat does it mean? how does it interact with monster  behavior?\n### [3.2 Chase](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#Chases)\nWhat is the purpose of a chase?\n### [3.4 Creating a creature](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#CreatingaCreature)\nMonkeying with monsters what does fiddling with different parts of a statblock mean\n- Minor alterations\n- Major alteration\n### [3.8 Death](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#Death)\n- Fairness\n- Memorability\n### [3.9 Doors](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#Doors)\nAs vox machina can tell you, doors are a staple of good D&D.\n### [3.11 Environmental effects](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#EnvironmentalEffects)\nThis is purely tool for DMs to add more meaning to their environments \n### [3.17 Mass combat](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#Mobs)\nMobs and how to use them in a heroic setting.\n### [3.18 NPC's](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/dms-toolbox#DetailedNPCs)\nHow to use NPCs and have them appear without causing problems.\n### [4.0 Adventure Creation](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/dmg-2024/creating-adventures)\nHow to create an adventure\n## Story System\n### Problem Statement\nIn a game of make belief, why do we have character levels, dice, CR, etc in the first place? They are communication devices, which let the players signal their strength and success. In a campaign, DM'ing is a lonesome job, no one to discuss your plans with and no one to scheme with, however, one benefit of this style of play is that because it is a single DM the world remains consistent game after game.\n\nWhat about a westmarch though? With dozens of DMs working in the same world together? How the hell do they communicate with each other and keep the world consistent so that it may feel real and immersive to the players?\n### Solution\nThe answer is that similar to how players are tied to certain classes and mechanics so that they may communicate in a way the game system understands, the DMs need certain mechanics through which they can communicate that the westmarch understands. Aka the Story system.\n\nWe want you to open a portal to the abyss! we want you to rain zombies! Whatever it is that you can imagine, we can support. But to make sure all DMs are on the same playing field and can actually collaborate, there needs to some sort of standardization. You can only break the status quo if there is one.\n### Promise\nThis is what awaits you, all DMs earn story points by simply DM'ing games. From there, you can claim a special antagonist, a villain or an NPC that can become a villain or an ally. Spending story points lets you break all kinds of rules and make grand moves against the PCs. However, this time around you can find aid in other DMs and their villains & NPCs, collaborations and backstabbing, all done in a manner which the server understands and encourages.\n\nGo ahead and commit war crimes, learn more about story powers on the [DM Mechanics](/rules/guides/dm-mechanics) Page. If you have any questions at all reach out to @DMMentors they will guide you.\n\n## If you feel like you are ready to begin your DM journey, go open up a DM Approval (DMA) ticket [here](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1278900273804476539/1367600232652734524)\n", "category": "Systems", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"👓\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"A guide to DMing in our community.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "3c86821f-a019-5799-8a50-3d5926da3a54", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "dungeon-master-s-guide", "status": "published", "title": "Dungeon Master's Guide", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "Each character has 3 deaths, every time they die, they mark one of these deaths. Once a character has no more deaths remaining, they are permanently dead, beyond all resurrection.\n\nHowever, while a character has any deaths remaining, they cannot permanently die. If a character would permanently die, they instead follow the following conditions.\n\n• Whatever remains of their body returns back to the agora. \n• If nothing would remain of their body, a strand of hair still remains and returns.  \n• If something would consume their souls, their souls instead escape.\n", "category": "Systems", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"☠️\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules to deal with character death.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "f3f8ccd4-ff53-5c6f-b5dc-be4f9d1a1889", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "death-system", "status": "published", "title": "Death System", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "**Downtime Projects** are what your character does when they are outside of games to prepare for their next adventure.\n\nEvery long rest you get 1 downtime quest (**DTQ**) per character you have, for a maximum of 2 per player. You can spend DTQs to make progress in your Downtime Projects.\n\nIf you only have 1 Character active on the server, that character gets 2 DTQs per long rest.\n\nDTQs reset at every replenishment and do not stack.\n\nThere are two kinds of projects you can spend DTQs on - **Quick Projects** and **Passion Projects**.\n\nQuick Projects are designed to beginner friendly and easy to pickup and understand while still being very useful, Passion Projects on the other hand are bit more crunchier and require some reading.\n\n## Quick Projects\nQuick Projects always only take 1 DTQ, aka your character completes them instantaneously. Each quick project tells you the rules associated with it and what benefits you gain from the project.\n## How to do Quick Projects?\n- Go to the downtime channel here.\n- Copy and paste the DTQ line of the project you are doing.\n\n## Brewing Potions\n**Tool Prerequisite** - Proficiency in Herbalism Kit\n\n| **Name**                   | **Gold Cost (GP)** |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Potion of Healing          | 25                 |\n| Potion of Greater Healing  | 50                 |\n| Potion of Superior Healing | 100                |\n\nYou can spend up to 100 GP in 1 DTQ in this Quick Project and acquire healing potions appropriately.\n\nExample - A Character could spend 100 GP and get 2 Potions of Healing and 1 Potion of Greater Healing.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Brewing Healing Potions - Spending X gold to gain Y potions`\n## Collect Rumors\nPrerequisite - DM Approval\n\nChoose a quest that your character is going to play in, and ask the DM any 3 questions about this quest. The DM adjudicates whether the questions you asked could be answered through rumors, if some questions don’t qualify you can ask new questions. The DM then answers you with rumors your character has managed to collect.\n\nTwo of the three answers are true, one is false, your character won’t be able to verify which is which until they play in the game.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Collect Rumors - @DM of the game - link of the game post`\n## Copy New Spells\n**Class Prerequisite** - Wizard\n\nA Wizard Character can copy spells from another Wizard’s spell book or a Spell Scroll so long as the spell is on the Wizard’s Spell List.\n\nA Wizard can copy spells up to their Intelligence Modifier in one Quick Project. For each spell they copy they must spend 50 GP per spell level of the spell. For example a third level spell requires 150 GP to copy.\n\nHowever based on the Subclass of the Wizard they can copy certain Spells at 10 GP per spell level rather than 50. The following table lists the Spells for each Subclass.\n\n| Subclass    | Spells                       |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Abjurer     | Any Abjuration Spell         |\n| Bladesinger | Any Spell with Range of Self |\n| Conjurer    | Any Conjuration Spell        |\n| Diviner     | Any Divination Spell         |\n| Enchanter   | Any Enchantment Spell        |\n| Evoker      | Any Evocation Spell          |\n| Illusionist | Any Illusion Spell           |\n| Necromancer | Any Necromancy Spell         |\n| Transmuter  | Any Transmutation Spell      |\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Copying New Spells - Spending X Gold to Copy Y spells from Z as the source.`\n## Craft Mundane Item\n**Tool Prerequisite** - Smith’s Tools\n\nChoose any one piece of Adventuring Gear that is of the types - Weapon or Armor. You can spend gold up to half it’s purchase cost and craft the item instead of purchasing it.\n\nExample - Plate Armor costs 1500 GP to purchase, so you can spend 750 GP to craft it using this Quick Project instead.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Crafting Mundane Item - Spending X Gold to Craft Y Item.`\n## Craft Magic Item\n**Tool Prerequisite** - Tinker’s Tools\n\nChoose one unlocked magic item recipe, spend the relics required in the recipe.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Crafting Magic Item - Choosing X Recipe, Spending Y Relics`\n## Gift Soul Bound Item\nIf you have a Magic Item that is soul bound according to the Server Rules as mentioned here - [Magic Items](/rules/guides/magic-items), you can do this Quick Project to Unbound the item and gift it to another character.\n\nThe Item becomes Soul Bound to that Character instead.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Gifting a soul bound item - From Character X to Character Y.`\n## Prepare Spells\nIf you play as class that can prepare new spells every long rest, you can take this Quick Project to prepare your spell list again as if you had just completed a long rest.\n\nFor classes that can normally only change 1 spell per long rest, they can change all prepared spells instead.\n\nClasses Effected - Artificer, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Wizard\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Preparing New Spells.`\n## Recovery\nWhen you use the Recovery Quick Project, you can spend a certain amount of gold to activate any one of the following options.\n\nPB stands for Proficiency Bonus.\n\n- You can spend **10 x PB** gold and get back **PB** hit die.\n- You can spend **15 x PB** gold and get back **PB** hit die and a combined level of spell slots equal to **PB**.\n\nExample - A Wizard can spend 45 GP and get back 3 Hit Dice and 3 Spell Slot Levels, so they can recover a 3rd Level Spell Slot or a 2nd Level Slot and a 1st Level Slot.\n\nAny Character can take Short Rests and spend Hit Dice to heal themselves as noted in Short Rest rules.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Recovering - Spending X Gold, Recovering Y Hit dice, Z spell slots.`\n## Scribe Cantrip or First Level Scrolls\n**Tool Prerequisite** - Calligrapher’s Supplies\n\n**Gold Prerequisite** - 25 GP\n\nA character who has access to a Cantrip or First Level spell can use this quick project to make a Spell Scroll of the same Cantrip.\n\nThe Spell Scroll uses the creator’s Spell Attack modifier and Spell DC.\n\nYou can spend up to a 100 GP on this Quick Project and make spell scrolls appropriately.\n\nExample - A Character with the True Strike and Blade Ward Cantrips can spend 75 GP to create 2 scrolls of True Strike and 1 scroll of Blade Ward.\n\nDTQ Line - `@downtime Quick Project - Scribing Cantrip or First Level Scrolls - Spending X Gold to Scribe Y Scrolls.`\n", "category": "Systems", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🕰️\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Rules about Quick Projects aka the simple downtime system.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "05220041-4063-51f6-88be-b5fa70aefffc", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "quick-projects", "status": "published", "title": "Downtime System (Quick Projects)", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "## Dice\nWhile playing any game in this server, you must use the Avrae bot to roll in the VC chat of the gameroom you are playing in. If you are not familiar with avrae check out the [Bots Guide](/rules/guides/bots-guide).\n## Time\n**Game Week starts** - Thursdays 5:30 AM IST. \n## Resting\n- **Long Rest** - Happens at Thursdays 5:30 AM IST for all characters. No other long rests are available.\n- **Short Rests** - 2 per week, Instantaneous outside of a session, can be taken within a session with DM permission, takes 1 hour of game time.\n## Equipment\n- **Purchase**: All mundane equipment (aka everything listed in adventuring gear of the PHB that is not a magic item) can be bought for actual price as listed in D&D Beyond.\n- **Sale**: All the above can also be **sold at half price.**\n- **Tracking**: Just remove the gold from your DDB, and add the items as needed.\n- **Ammunition**: We don’t track any kinds of mundane ammunition on the server, so long as you have a bundle of arrows, bolts or a bag of gun or sling bullets we assume you have enough ammunition to keep shooting.\n- **Armor**: The prices of plate armor in the server are Full Plate - 750 gp, Half plate - 375 gp, Breastplate - 200 gp, Splint - 125 gp.\n## Buffs\n- Buffs from non-party members such as class abilities, spells etc. may be given to a party going on a quest. Let your DM know of this in advance. Ultimately it is up to the DM to allow this or not. \n- Any buffs that last for any duration which is not **Untill Dispelled/Till the next long rest** are only active for 1 session. Buffs that do last untill dispelled or till the next long rest can retain over multiple sessions.\n- Heroic Inspiration provided by a DM is considered a buff and lasts until used.\n## Text Roleplay\nPutting yourself in your characters boots while adventuring not enough?\n\nChannels such as **rp-agora** allow you to roleplay your character between adventures and interact with other player characters and on occasion, other NPCs! Here is how you can engage with text roleplay on this server and some base assumptions that we operate with:\n\n- A character can be in one location at any given time.\n- Time jumps are not allowed.\n- Read the pinned messages to know what the scene/setting is.\n- Be mindful to indicate when your character is entering/leaving the area.\n- Read up a little before joining or ask for clarification in ooc - [Out of Character channel](https://discord.com/channels/1278898468970299523/1426857895017975859).\n- DMs can open limited time RP scenes where you may interact with whatever the scene might be but remember the access to such is limited and controlled by the DM.\n\n## Voice Roleplay\nNot a fan of roleplaying on text?\n\n- You can hop on with friends on a voice channel and start roleplaying! You can only do this if all the characters involved are in the same location at the same time.\n- You need a DM to witness any voice roleplay tomake sure the roleplay remains within the bounds of the setting.\n- If spectating others, treat it like any other session and remain muted and respect the tone of the scene when sending messages in the side chat.\n- Reminder that all forms of Roleplay must adhere to server lines and veils as mentioned [here](https://chronicler.smokebombstudios.com/rules/guides/community-rules)\n## Game Rewards\nThe XP you earn for each game is associated with your character level. You gain XP proportionate to your character level, as per the table below. If you have failed to achieve the objective for a session, you gain no XP, this is adjudicated by the DM of the session. \n\n### XP per Level\n\n| Lvl | XP   |\n| --- | ---- |\n| 3   | 600  |\n| 4   | 800  |\n| 5   | 1000 |\n| 6   | 1200 |\n| 7   | 1400 |\n| 8   | 1600 |\n| 9   | 1800 |\n| 10  | 2000 |\n**Monster Equipment** - Unless the DM says otherwise all the equipment a monster has is by default rendered unusable and worthless.\n## Additional Rewards\n- **Gold** - If gold is found within a game it is divided equally amongst all the players.\n- **Recipes** - If a magic item recipe is found within a game it just unlocks the recipe for the entire server, the party gets the bragging rights to bring it home.\n- **Relics & Magic Items** - At the end of the session, each player involved calls out a Need, Greed or Pass for each of these items. Passers are skipped and Need beats greed. In case of a tie, first compare Pity points, the one with the highest Pity takes the item, if the tie still persists everyone rolls a d20 to break it. \n- Any player who didn't get the item gets 1 pity point. Pity is reset to 0 whenever you gain one of these items through this distribution. Pity is tracked per player.\n## Level Cap\nCharacter progression in the community is capped at level 10. For progress after that check out [PCXP](/rules/guides/pcxp).\n", "category": "Systems", "frontmatter_yaml": "emoji: \"🎲\"\nwip: \"false\"\nsummary: \"Gameplay Rules that apply to each game.\"\n", "kind": "rule", "public_id": "49e723fa-1b3c-5952-ac86-9c0e62b6b7b3", "published_at": "2026-10-25T00:00:00Z", "slug": "gameplay-guide", "status": "published", "title": "Gameplay Guide", "version": 1, "visibility": "public"}, "table": "documents"}
{"conflict": ["slug"], "refs": {"author_id": {"platform_owner": true, "table": "members"}}, "row": {"body": "Magic items, we know em, we love em. In the server you can find magic items by defeating villains, going into dungeons etc. To make sure the magic items do not destroy the mental peace of our dear DMs we have the following limits on the magic items within the server.\n## Categories\n- **Consumables:** Free. No limit. (Potions, scrolls, ammo)\n- **Permanent Items:** Any permanent item, automatically **soul bound**.\n\nAll permanent magic items are soul bound to the current holder. To transfer a permanent item one of the players involved must use a Downtime Quest (DTQ). What does soul bound mean? Explained below.\n\n**Common Items are an exception to this rule and are treated the same as Consumables.**\n## Carry Limit = Level Tier\n\n| **Level** | **Magic Items You Can Use** |\n| --------- | --------------------------- |\n| 3 - 4     | 1 Item                      |\n| 5 - 6     | 2 Items                     |\n| 7 - 8     | 3 Items                     |\n| 9 - 10    | 4 Items                     |\n\n## Soul Bound\nA soul bound item is bound to the soul of one character and can only be used by that character and cannot be freely transferred and traded and must instead follow the special rules as listed below.\n\n- You can carry up to your limit of **Soul bound** items.\n- Gifting one requires a **DTQ**.\n- Soul bound items may reflect your class, alignment, or story.\n- The person who uses the item first becomes the holder.\n## Crafting\nWithin the setting of weeping you will find a new kind of resource, called **Relics**. There are 3 types of relics - Blade Relics, Plate Relics and Rune Relics. As you play games you will find relics as quest rewards. \n\n**Flavor** - These relics are pieces of technology left behind from the age of heroes. While we have lost the knowledge required to restore such wonders, we have figured out a way to repurpose the latent magic that is still strong within them into making our own useful trinkets. That is if we find the recipes needed to do so.\n\nA Recipe is a resource that tells you how many relics of what kind you need to make the item. The player base as a whole unlocks a recipe whenever any players find a recipe as a quest reward.\n## How to Craft Magic Items?\n- You do the Craft a Magic Item DTQ\n- Choose an unlocked recipe\n- Spend the appropriate amount of relics to make the item\n## Unlocked Recipes\n\n| Item                                              | Rarity    | Blade | Plate | Rune |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | --------- | ----- | ----- | ---- |\n| Armor of Gleaming                                 | Common    | 0     | 1     | 0    |\n| Bead of Nourishment                               | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Bead of Refreshment                               | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Boots of False Tracks                             | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Candle of the Deep                                | Common    | 0     | 1     | 0    |\n| Cast-Off Armor                                    | Common    | 0     | 1     | 0    |\n| Charlatan's Die                                   | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Cloak of Billowing                                | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Cloak of Many Fashions                            | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Clockwork Amulet                                  | Common    | 1     | 0     | 0    |\n| Clothes of Mending                                | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Conjurer's Canopy                                 | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Dark Shard Amulet                                 | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Dictation Quill                                   | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Dread Helm                                        | Common    | 0     | 1     | 0    |\n| Ear Horn of Hearing                               | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Elocutionist's Lexicon                            | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Enduring Spellbook                                | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Ensorcelled Missive                               | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Ersatz Eye                                        | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Evergreen Fertilizer                              | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Hat of Vermin                                     | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Hat of Wizardry                                   | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Heward's Handy Spice Pouch                        | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Homeward Compass                                  | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Horn of Silent Alarm                              | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Instrument of Illusions                           | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Instrument of Scribing                            | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Lock of Trickery                                  | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Lucky Foot                                        | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Manifold Tool                                     | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Moon-Touched Sword                                | Common    | 1     | 0     | 0    |\n| Mystery Key                                       | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Orb of Direction                                  | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Orb of Time                                       | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Perfume of Bewitching                             | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    |\n| Pipe of Smoke Monsters                            | Common    | 0     | 0     | 1    